<div id=3D"spae01f3c9024ac49a10" class=3D"text_spoiler" style=3D"display: n=
one;">
<div class=3D"contenteditable">
<p><br></p>
<p>This method is designed to install controller drivers, WLAN drivers, net=
work drivers, etc.<br>Note: This method is not intended for installing very=
 large drivers such as video etc... as it will significantly increase the W=
inPE boot time.<br>The drivers should be in unpacked form, i.e. driver *.sy=
s, security directory *.cat, and *.inf file, i.e. it should not be an .exe =
file installer.<br>If necessary, you can pack the drivers into 7-Zip archiv=
es.</p>
<p>In order for your drivers to be installed when loading WinPE, place them=
 on your bootable USB flash drive, in the SSTR/USER folder, in the appropri=
ate subfolder. They will be installed automatically. Subfolders are allowed=
.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><br></p>
<p><b><span style=3D"color:#2969b0;">Adding your own commands to cmd or bat=
