one;">
<div class=3D"contenteditable">On it is searched and launched (if found) wi=
ndows\system32\boot\winload.exe. The option is not a panacea for the treatm=
ent ... but it will help to load the Windows if the MBR/PBR entries are dam=
aged, the bootmgr bootloader on the HDD, its BCD menu, other files from the=
 boot partition, or the problem with the partition itself. After the OS is =
booted (it can boot up unactivated - this is normal, depends on the activat=
ion method), it will only be necessary to restore the boot files (if they w=
ere, of course, damaged) by regular or third-party utilities. Without speci=
al need, this method is not recommended.</div>
</div>
</div>
